t with More Credit Where to Send Your Transcripts Pursue Your Next Degree Application Requirements Business Health Sciences Liberal Arts Nursing Public Service Technology International Students Start Here Tuition and Aid Tuition Undergraduate Tuition Graduate Tuition Military Tuition Veteran Tuition Financial Aid NYS Free Tuition Eligibility Federal Financial Aid Steps to Apply for Financial Aid NY State Financial Aid for Residents Excelsior University Scholarships Grant and Private Loan Opportunities Resources Documents and Forms Payment Plans Resources Resources & Services Academic Calendar Accommodations for Students Bookstore & More Career Readiness Excelsior University Library Honor Societies at Excelsior National Cybersecurity Institute (NCI) Registration and Records Tech Support Web and Digital Accessibility The Writing Center Transcript Requests Online Transcript Request for Students and Alumni OneTranscript® Service for Non-Excelsior Students Military and Veteran Resources Military and Veteran Education Veterans Center Program Catalogs Catalogs Start With More Credit Start With More Credit ACE/Credly Transcripts Credit For Credit for Business and Professional Certifications Credit for Criminal Justice Training Credit for Educational and Vocational Programs Credit for Health Care Credentials Credit for IT Certifications, Training, and Exams Credit for Military Experience Credit For Nuclear Utility Accredited Training Programs Credit for Nursing Certifications and Licenses Credit for Professional and Workplace Training Credit for College and University Professional Training About Institutional Information About Excelsior About Our Students St. Petersburg Site Accreditations Contact Information Justice, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion Excelsior University EthicsHub Institutional Review Board Leadership Fast Facts George H. Atkinson Center at Excelsior University Media and Publications Life at Excelsior Blog Excelsior University Magazine Excelsior University Newsroom Faculty and Staff Published Works Academic Program Catalogs Center for Executive and Professional Education Center for Social Justice Calendar of Events Commencement Jobs at Excelsior University Policies and Guidelines Transparency Academic Transparency Administrative Transparency Regulatory Transparency Search search Fall II starts October 26. Ready to begin? Contact Admissions today. × Request Info Apply Call Us CLOSE Call Us For general inquiries, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Director, Allied Health Programs Jobs at Excelsior University Director, Allied Health Programs Status Full Time Location Remote Apply Now View All Jobs Build the next generation of allied health workforce programs at Excelsior, creating innovative pathways that connect learners with high-demand healthcare careers and employers with skilled talent. The Director, Allied Health Programs provides entrepreneurial, operational, and academic leadership for the development, launch, growth, and continuous improvement of noncredit allied health workforce programs within Excelsior University's Center for Executive and Professional Education (CEPE). The Director's initial priority will be developing and delivering hybrid Medical Assistant and/or Certified Nursing Assistant certification-preparation programming that combines online learning with hands-on laboratory education at Excelsior's St. Petersburg, Florida location. The Director will subsequently evaluate and develop additional high-demand allied health offerings based on workforce demand, employer needs, regulatory feasibility, student outcomes, and financial sustainability. Reporting to the Associate Vice President, CEPE, this role works cross-functionally with compliance, academic affairs, legal, finance, marketing, enrollment, facilities, technology, and student support to create marketable, compliant, scalable programs that prepare learners for industry certifications and employment. This position may be filled in a remote or hybrid capacity, with preference for candidates in the St. Petersburg area. Regular presence in St. Petersburg and regional and national travel, including occasional weekends and overnight travel, may be required.' Duties and Responsibilities: •Lead the design, approval, launch, operation, and growth of CEPE's allied health portfolio, beginning with Medical Assistant and/or Certified Nursing Assistant programming. •Develop a multi-year allied health portfolio strategy informed by workforce demand, employer needs, regulatory requirements, competitive analysis, and financial sustainability. •Develop program business cases, budgets, enrollment forecasts, pricing recommendations, implementation plans, risk assessments, and performance dashboards. •Ensure curricula, laboratory experiences, assessments, policies, staffing, and student disclosures align with certification, employer, institutional, and regulatory requirements.]•Lead regulatory, compliance, accreditation, and certification-related activities in collaboration with institutional stakeholders. •Establish and maintain laboratory safety, competency verification, equipment, supply, incident-response, and operational procedures. •Recruit, supervise, evaluate, and develop instructors, subject-matter experts, and program support personnel. •Build partnerships with healthcare employers, workforce organizations, and community partners to support program design, experiential learning, and employment pathways. •Establish and lead an allied health employer advisory structure. •Partner with marketing, enrollment, and student-support teams on recruitment, onboarding, retention, certification support, and career readiness. •Monitor enrollment, retention, completion, certification, employment, satisfaction, revenue, expense, and contribution-margin performance and drive continuous improvement. •Identify employer, workforce, public, philanthropic, and grant-funded opportunities to expand access and support program growth. Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited institution in allied health, healthcare administration, education, workforce development, business, or a related field, or substantial directly relevant allied health program leadership, clinical education, workforce development, or business-building experience. At least seven years of progressively responsible experience in allied health education, healthcare workforce development, career and technical education, clinical program operations, or a closely related field, including at least three years of leadership, supervisory, or program-management responsibility. The successful candidate will demonstrate experience developing, launching, managing, or growing allied health, healthcare workforce, career education, or certification-preparation programs. Candidates should possess working knowledge of entry-level allied health occupations and certification pathways and be able to translate certification standards, employer expectations, and regulatory requirements into effective curricula, laboratory experiences, policies, staffing models, and student practices. Experience with hybrid or online education, clinical or laboratory safety, faculty supervision, employer partnerships, budgeting, program profitability, project management, and data-informed decision-making is required. The successful candidate must demonstrate strong written and verbal communication, sound judgment, attention to detail, and the ability to work effectively across institutional functions in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment. Proficiency with learning management, student information, CRM, reporting, and collaboration technologies is expected. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in a related field; current or previously held healthcare license or nationally recognized allied health certification Experience launching new programs and achieving measurable enrollment, completion, certification, employment, or financial outcomes; Experience with Florida postsecondary education, workforce training, healthcare employers, regulatory requirements, the Florida Commission for Independent Education, national certification organizations, clinical affiliation agreements, or allied health programmatic accreditation. The hiring salary range for this position is $80,000.00 - $90,000.00. The hiring salary range above represents the University's good faith estimate at the time of posting Application Information Applicants must reside in the United States and be authorized to work in the U.S. If you experience any issues with the online submission process, please email recruitment@excelsior.edu . Excelsior University offers competitive compensation and a generous benefits package that includes paid time off, retirement, and excellent health insurance. Interested candidates should submit a letter of application, resume, and the names of three professional references. Please submit requested information by clicking the Apply Now button on this page. AA/EOE/ADA Excelsior University is an equal opportunity employer committed to ensuring all qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to any legally protected characteristic. Apply Now View All Jobs Jobs filler MyExcelsior Support Resources Areas of Study Tuition and Aid Admissions About Contact Us Jobs at Excelsior Excelsior University Main Campus 7 Columbia Circle Albany, NY 12203-5159 Educational Site 9400 4th Street N., Suite 100 St. Petersburg, FL 33702 © 2026 Excelsior University • Privacy • Policies • Transparency at Excelsior • Campus Safety • Title IX • Accommodations • Accessibility • Help • Feedback Start your degree with courses in Spanish. Learn about our ¡Adelante! program CLOSE Which language do you prefer? View our site in English or Spanish. English Español CLOSE Site Tools Stop Animations Start Animations Show Form Labels Hide Form Labels Accessibility at Excelsior We believe in education for all. Sitemap Technical Help Accessibility Statement More about Accessibility at Excelsior"
