ns, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Chief Marketing Officer Jobs at Excelsior University Chief Marketing Officer Status Full Time Location Albany, NY Apply Now View All Jobs The Chief Marketing Officer (CMO) will lead Excelsior University's strategy for enrollment marketing, lead generation, overall brand and student pipeline growth. This position is solely responsible for building brand awareness and demand generation for the University's degree and non-degree programs and for developing the marketing strategies, campaigns, and channels that generate qualified inquiries and grow the prospective student pipeline. This role does not oversee admissions, registrar, academic advising, student financial services, or other enrollment management operations; it is a dedicated marketing role. Enrollment Marketing operates as part of Excelsior's shared services unit, and this position will lead the team in an agency model — meaning that, while the CMO will focus first and foremost on academic program prospective student inquiries for Excelsior University, they will also have responsibility for delivering marketing and lead-generation services to other members of the University's network. The CMO will play a key role in the exciting opportunity to grow this network by growing shared services revenues by identifying and securing new network partners and by expanding the services sold to existing partners. As an executive leader on the Excelsior team reporting to the President, this position will be expected to strategize, execute, and manage a high-performing marketing team, and to work in close collaboration with Admissions and Academic Affairs, Communications and other University and network partners, to translate marketing-generated interest into a strong, well-qualified applicant pipeline. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following: Other duties may be assigned Own student pipeline growth: set clear, measurable goals for inquiry volume, lead quality, conversion to application, and cost per lead/acquisition, and report progress against those goals to executive leadership. Lead and manage the marketing team, including digital marketing, content/brand marketing, product marketing, and marketing operations and analytics staff. Lead Enrollment Marketing's operation as a shared service, delivering marketing and lead-generation services to other members of the University's network under an agency model, with clear service agreements, deliverables, and pricing. Grow shared services revenue by identifying, pursuing, and onboarding new network partners, and by expanding the scope of services sold to existing partners (upselling and cross-selling additional marketing services). Own the shared services P&L, including pricing strategy, cost-to-serve, and profitability by partner, and report on shared services growth and performance to the President and executive leadership. Develop and execute an integrated enrollment marketing strategy — spanning digital, content, paid, organic, and offline channels — to build brand awareness and drive qualified lead generation for all degree and non-degree programs. Collaborate closely with the Admissions unit to ensure a seamless handoff of marketing-generated leads into the admissions funnel, aligning on lead scoring, service-le"
    },
