 and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Admissions Counselor Jobs at Excelsior University Admissions Counselor Status Full Time Location Albany, NY Apply Now View All Jobs The Admissions Counselor plays a key role in ensuring prospective students are at the heart of everything we do at Excelsior University. As a dedicated admissions consultant, this position builds meaningful relationships with prospective students, understands their educational and career goals, identifies needs and barriers, and guides students toward the Excelsior University program and enrollment pathway that best fits their goals. The Admissions Counselor serves as both a trusted advisor and an enrollment professional. Using a consultative approach, the counselor engages prospective students in meaningful conversations, assesses needs and readiness, communicates the value of Excelsior's programs, addresses questions and concerns, creates appropriate urgency, and helps students take meaningful next steps toward enrollment. The Admissions Counselor owns and actively manages an assigned prospective student pipeline and is accountable for effective outreach, follow-up, engagement, and progression through the admissions process while maintaining the highest standards of student service, integrity, compliance, and ethical recruitment. We believe work should fit your life, not the other way around. While this position is primarily based in Albany, NY, with a hybrid schedule that includes two days in the office and the flexibility to work from home on other days, remote work options may also be considered. This is a full-time, 37.5-hour-per-week, 12-month, benefits-eligible position. Work hours may vary between 8:30 AM and 8:00 PM, Monday through Friday, and may include rotating Saturday hours. Schedules are subject to change based on the needs of the University and its students. Key Responsibilities Consultative Enrollment & Relationship Building Build trusting, meaningful relationships with prospective students while maintaining accountability for enrollment progression. Use active listening, thoughtful questioning, and needs analysis to understand students' goals, motivations, circumstances, and barriers. Recommend appropriate programs, pathways, and resources based on each student's individual needs and goals. Clearly communicate the features, benefits, value, requirements, and costs of Excelsior University programs. Address questions, concerns, objections, and barriers with confidence, empathy, and accurate information. Help students establish clear next steps, timelines, and commitments toward enrollment. Pipeline Management & Enrollment Goals Take ownership of an assigned prospective student pipeline from initial inquiry through application, admission, and enrollment. Conduct consistent and purposeful outreach and follow-up based on student engagement, readiness, enrollment stage, and established contact strategies. Prioritize outreach based on student intent, upcoming start dates, outstanding requirements, and opportunities for progression. Identify stalled or disengaged students and implement appropriate strategies to re-engage them. Achieve established individual and team activity, productivity, and enrollment goals. Use CRM and performance data to monitor pipeline activity, prioritize work, ide"
    },
