ctional strategies, tools, and assessments to achieve identified learning outcomes. • Ensure course content aligns with Excelsior’s course design standards, accessibility guidelines, and online learning best practices. • Partner with media developers to create high-quality course materials, including videos, simulations, and interactive elements. • Review and refine course content to ensure clarity, coherence, and alignment with learning objectives. • Collaborate with other instructional designers to enhance Excelsior’s course development methodologies and resources. Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. • Bachelor’s degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technology, or a related field. • 3+ years’ experience designing and developing online courses for higher education. • Strong knowledge of instructional design models (e.g., Backward Design, Bloom’s Taxonomy). • Strong relationship-building skills. • Familiarity with best practices for online learning and adult education. • Ability to guide SMEs in structuring content for effective online delivery. • Experience with learning management systems (LMS), preferably Canvas. • Strong written and verbal communication skills. • Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. • Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications: • Master’s degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technology, or a related field. • Experience developing courses for non-traditional, adult learners. • Prior experience working in a centralized course development model. • Proficiency in accessibility standards and universal design for learning (UDL). • Experience using data and learner analytics to infor"
