t with More Credit Where to Send Your Transcripts Pursue Your Next Degree Application Requirements Business Health Sciences Liberal Arts Nursing Public Service Technology International Students Start Here Tuition and Aid Tuition Undergraduate Tuition Graduate Tuition Military Tuition Veteran Tuition Financial Aid NYS Free Tuition Eligibility Federal Financial Aid Steps to Apply for Financial Aid NY State Financial Aid for Residents Excelsior University Scholarships Grant and Private Loan Opportunities Resources Documents and Forms Payment Plans Resources Resources & Services Academic Calendar Accommodations for Students Bookstore & More Career Readiness Excelsior University Library Honor Societies at Excelsior National Cybersecurity Institute (NCI) Registration and Records Tech Support Web and Digital Accessibility The Writing Center Transcript Requests Online Transcript Request for Students and Alumni OneTranscript® Service for Non-Excelsior Students Military and Veteran Resources Military and Veteran Education Veterans Center Program Catalogs Catalogs Start With More Credit Start With More Credit ACE/Credly Transcripts Credit For Credit for Business and Professional Certifications Credit for Criminal Justice Training Credit for Educational and Vocational Programs Credit for Health Care Credentials Credit for IT Certifications, Training, and Exams Credit for Military Experience Credit For Nuclear Utility Accredited Training Programs Credit for Nursing Certifications and Licenses Credit for Professional and Workplace Training Credit for College and University Professional Training About Institutional Information About Excelsior About Our Students St. Petersburg Site Accreditations Contact Information Justice, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion Excelsior University EthicsHub Institutional Review Board Leadership Fast Facts George H. Atkinson Center at Excelsior University Media and Publications Life at Excelsior Blog Excelsior University Magazine Excelsior University Newsroom Faculty and Staff Published Works Academic Program Catalogs Center for Executive and Professional Education Center for Social Justice Calendar of Events Commencement Jobs at Excelsior University Policies and Guidelines Transparency Academic Transparency Administrative Transparency Regulatory Transparency Search search Fall II starts October 26. Ready to begin? Contact Admissions today. × Request Info Apply Call Us CLOSE Call Us For general inquiries, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Senior Director- Human Resources Jobs at Excelsior University Senior Director- Human Resources Status Full Time Location Albany, NY Apply Now View All Jobs The Senior Director of Human Resources is a strategic leadership role responsible for supporting the operational excellence, organizational effectiveness, and people-centered culture of the University. Reporting to the Vice President for Human Resources, the Senior Director serves as a key advisor and operational leader within the HR department, helping ensure efficient and responsive HR services that support the institution’s mission, values, and strategic priorities. This hybrid position requires exceptional communication, organizational leadership, strategic planning, and project management skills. The Senior Director partners closely with university leadership, governance groups, and other departments  to foster productive working relationships, strengthen organizational culture, and advance the University as an employer of choice. The Senior Director supports multiple functional areas within Human Resources, including employee relations, payroll, benefits, talent acquisition, learning and development, HR operations, and budget oversight. The role also represents Human Resources in institutional governance, strategic planning initiatives, and cross-functional leadership efforts. Key Responsibilities Strategic Leadership & HR Operations Partner with the Vice President for Human Resources to develop and implement strategic HR initiatives aligned with institutional priorities. Support the effective daily operations of the HR department and ensure high-quality service delivery across HR functions. Represent Human Resources in university governance, strategic planning activities, councils and task forces, risk assessment and business continuity efforts, and institutional initiatives. Lead and manage complex HR projects and organizational initiatives from planning through execution. Analyze organizational trends, workforce needs, and HR metrics to support data-informed decision-making. Employee Relations & Organizational Effectiveness Supports employee relations efforts and provides guidance on performance management, conflict resolution, workplace investigations, policy interpretation, and employee concerns. Promote a positive, inclusive, and collaborative workplace culture that reflects institutional values. Mentor and coach managers and supervisors on leadership effectiveness, employee engagement, and talent development. Support initiatives that strengthen employee morale, retention, and organizational trust. Assist in cultivating a workplace environment recognized as a best place to work. Leadership Development & Talent Management Support leadership development and succession planning initiatives across the institution. Help identify and nurture internal talent through mentoring, coaching, and professional development strategies. Collaborate with HR leadership to advance learning and development programs for faculty, staff, and supervisors. Partner with talent acquisition efforts to support strategic recruitment and workforce planning initiatives. Budget & Administrative Oversight Assist with development, management, and oversight of the Human Resources budget. Monitor expenditures and support fiscally responsible operations within the HR department. Contribute to policy development, compliance efforts, and operational process improvements in collaboration with the Senior Director of HR Programs. Ensure HR practices align with applicable federal, state, and institutional regulations and policies in collaboration with the Senior Director of HR Programs and General Counsel. Collaboration & Partnership Build strong collaborative relationships with academic and administrative leaders across the University. Serve as a trusted advisor to leaders on organizational and workforce matters. Promote transparency, communication, and responsiveness within HR and across campus stakeholders. Support cross-functional collaboration to enhance employee experience and institutional effectiveness. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in human resources, Business Administration, Higher Education Administration, or a related field. Minimum of 5–10 years of progressively responsible Human Resources experience. Minimum of 3 years of HR leadership or management experience. Demonstrated experience in organizational leadership, employee relations, strategic planning, and project management. Strong understanding of HR operations, employment practices, and organizational development principles. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated ability to lead collaboratively in a complex organizational environment. Preferred Qualifications Human Resources experience within higher education or other complex institutional environments. Experience supporting shared governance structures and institutional strategic planning. Professional HR certification (e.g., SHRM-CP, SHRM-SCP, SPHR) preferred. Experience managing budgets and leading cross-functional initiatives. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strategic thinking and organizational leadership capabilities. Ability to manage multiple priorities and complex projects effectively. Strong conflict resolution, coaching, and consultation skills. High level of professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment. Ability to foster trust and maintain collaborative relationships across diverse constituencies. Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and employee engagement. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving abilities. Work Environment This position operates in a hybrid work environment and requires regular in office engagement with university leaders, employees, and stakeholders. Occasional evening or weekend responsibilities may be required to support institutional initiatives and events. The hiring salary range for this position is $110,000.00 - $120,000.00. The hiring salary range above represents the University's good faith estimate at the time of posting. Application Information Applicants must reside in the United States and be authorized to work in the U.S. If you experience any issues with the online submission process, please email recruitment@excelsior.edu . Excelsior University offers competitive compensation and a generous benefits package that includes paid time off, retirement, and excellent health insurance. Interested candidates should submit a letter of application, resume, and the names of three professional references. Please submit requested information by clicking the Apply Now button on this page. AA/EOE/ADA Excelsior University is an equal opportunity employer committed to ensuring all qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to any legally protected characteristic. Apply Now View All Jobs Jobs filler MyExcelsior Support Resources Areas of Study Tuition and Aid Admissions About Contact Us Jobs at Excelsior Excelsior University Main Campus 7 Columbia Circle Albany, NY 12203-5159 Educational Site 9400 4th Street N., Suite 100 St. Petersburg, FL 33702 © 2026 Excelsior University • Privacy • Policies • Transparency at Excelsior • Campus Safety • Title IX • Accommodations • Accessibility • Help • Feedback Start your degree with courses in Spanish. Learn about our ¡Adelante! program CLOSE Which language do you prefer? View our site in English or Spanish. English Español CLOSE Site Tools Stop Animations Start Animations Show Form Labels Hide Form Labels Accessibility at Excelsior We believe in education for all. Sitemap Technical Help Accessibility Statement More about Accessibility at Excelsior"
    },
