eneral inquiries, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Part-Time Adjunct Faculty – Nursing Success Coach Jobs at Excelsior University Part-Time Adjunct Faculty – Nursing Success Coach Status Part Time Location Remote Apply Now View All Jobs The Part-Time Adjunct Faculty – Nursing Success Coach is a remote, part-time faculty role within the School of Nursing that supports student progression, course success, remediation completion, and NCLEX readiness. Reporting to the appropriate Department Chair or academic leader, this position works with instructional faculty, School of Nursing leadership, academic support units, and student support services to provide structured, data-informed coaching for nursing students experiencing academic or progression challenges. Nursing Success Coaches engage students through scheduled coaching appointments, virtual office hours, small-group remediation, NCLEX-style question review, and study-skills support. They document student participation and progress, reinforce available academic resources, and contribute to engagement and retention efforts that promote persistence and academic achievement. The Nursing Success Coach provides academic coaching and support within established course and program expectations and does not independently modify course requirements, grading decisions, or progression requirements. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential duties and responsibilities include the following: Provide individualized academic coaching to nursing students identified through performance data, standardized assessment results, faculty referral, student self-referral, or other approved early-alert criteria. Use student performance indicators to identify needs for targeted academic support, remediation, or NCLEX readiness coaching. Facilitate coaching appointments, virtual office hours, small-group workshops, and academic support sessions focused on study strategies, test-taking skills, time management, clinical judgment, critical thinking, content review, and NCLEX-style question analysis. Support students in developing individualized success plans with clear goals, action steps, timelines, and follow-up expectations. Track coaching participation, remediation completion, progress toward success-plan goals, and other assigned student success indicators. Collaborate with instructional faculty to reinforce course expectations, support consistent remediation practices, and communicate student progress or concerns appropriately. Conduct NCLEX-style question review sessions and remediation activities aligned with course outcomes, program expectations, ATI resources, and student learning needs. Refer students to appropriate University resources, including academic advising, tutoring, accessibility services, library resources, wellness supports, or other services as appropriate. Maintain accurate documentation of coaching contacts, student progress, remediation activities, and outcomes using designated University systems or tracking tools. Provide trends, summaries, and recommendations to School of Nursing leadership as requested to support evaluation of student success initiatives. Complete University-required training, attend required pre-term or program meetings, and follow University policies, School of Nursing expectati"
    },
