s, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here FT Faculty-Clinical Education Lead Jobs at Excelsior University FT Faculty-Clinical Education Lead Status Full Time Location Albany, NY Apply Now View All Jobs Help shape the future of prelicensure nursing education by combining clinical teaching, faculty development and leadership, simulation and lab education, and healthcare partnership engagement across a growing clinical network. The Full-Time Faculty and Clinical Education Lead is a non-tenure track faculty position in the College of Nursing and Health Sciences. Reporting to the Assistant Dean, Lab and Clinical Education, this remote role supports prelicensure nursing education through clinical instruction, skills lab and simulation facilitation, student supervision, clinical faculty development, and clinical partner engagement. The faculty member serves as an academic and operational resource supporting implementation of the College's clinical education strategy and consistent, high-quality learning environments across clinical, laboratory, and simulation settings. The role collaborates with academic leadership, lab faculty, clinical operations, course faculty, part-time clinical instructors, and healthcare partners to advance student learning, faculty effectiveness, competency-based evaluation, clinical judgment, NCLEX-RN readiness, and clinical education quality. Preference will be given to candidates located in New York State or the Southeastern United States. Regular travel to clinical partner sites is required, with flexibility for clinical schedules, site visits, lab and simulation activities, and occasional evening or weekend commitments. This position is based out of the university’s home office in Albany, NY with the option of considering remote candidates. Remote employees will have mandatory occasional travel for meetings, conferences, and professional development opportunities. Remote employees are expected to be available during work hours 8:30 am – 5:00 pm Eastern time. The University will supply necessary equipment to perform the essential functions of this job (e.g., Laptop, docking station). Employees are responsible for having a workspace where they can participate in virtual meetings without multiple interruptions and noise. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach, facilitate, and evaluate prelicensure students in clinical, skills lab, and simulation environments. Provide direct clinical instruction based on program needs, faculty coverage, site requirements, and emerging priorities. Supervise and mentor students in safe nursing practice, clinical judgment, psychomotor skills, professionalism, and licensure readiness. Apply course outcomes, competency expectations, evaluation criteria, policies, and grading standards consistently. Identify and escalate student learning, safety, professionalism, and performance concerns; support remediation and student success strategies. Support recruitment, onboarding, orientation, development, mentoring, retention, and evaluation of part-time clinical instructors. Conduct clinical faculty observations, site visits, evaluations, and coaching; promote consistent clinical teaching and evaluation practices. Cultivate clinical partnerships through communication, site visits, needs assessment, timely follow-up, and c"
    },
