mic Calendar Start with More Credit Where to Send Your Transcripts Pursue Your Next Degree Application Requirements Business Health Sciences Liberal Arts Nursing Public Service Technology International Students Start Here Tuition and Aid Tuition Undergraduate Tuition Graduate Tuition Military Tuition Veteran Tuition Financial Aid NYS Free Tuition Eligibility Federal Financial Aid Steps to Apply for Financial Aid NY State Financial Aid for Residents Excelsior University Scholarships Grant and Private Loan Opportunities Resources Documents and Forms Payment Plans Resources Resources & Services Academic Calendar Accommodations for Students Bookstore & More Career Readiness Excelsior University Library Honor Societies at Excelsior National Cybersecurity Institute (NCI) Registration and Records Tech Support Web and Digital Accessibility The Writing Center Transcript Requests Online Transcript Request for Students and Alumni OneTranscript® Service for Non-Excelsior Students Military and Veteran Resources Military and Veteran Education Veterans Center Program Catalogs Catalogs Start With More Credit Start With More Credit ACE/Credly Transcripts Credit For Credit for Business and Professional Certifications Credit for Criminal Justice Training Credit for Educational and Vocational Programs Credit for Health Care Credentials Credit for IT Certifications, Training, and Exams Credit for Military Experience Credit For Nuclear Utility Accredited Training Programs Credit for Nursing Certifications and Licenses Credit for Professional and Workplace Training Credit for College and University Professional Training About Institutional Information About Excelsior About Our Students St. Petersburg Site Accreditations Contact Information Justice, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion Excelsior University EthicsHub Institutional Review Board Leadership Fast Facts George H. Atkinson Center at Excelsior University Media and Publications Life at Excelsior Blog Excelsior University Magazine Excelsior University Newsroom Faculty and Staff Published Works Academic Program Catalogs Center for Executive and Professional Education Center for Social Justice Calendar of Events Commencement Jobs at Excelsior University Policies and Guidelines Transparency Academic Transparency Administrative Transparency Regulatory Transparency Search search Fall II starts October 26. Ready to begin? Contact Admissions today. × Request Info Apply Call Us CLOSE Call Us For general inquiries, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Exec Director -BI, Data Platforms, and Applied AI Jobs at Excelsior University Exec Director -BI, Data Platforms, and Applied AI Status Full Time Location Albany, NY Apply Now View All Jobs The Executive Director of Data Engineering and Applied AI is a senior IT leader responsible for designing, developing, and executing Excelsior University’s enterprise data strategy. This includes the architecture, engineering, and operation of data platforms, integration frameworks, business intelligence solutions, and applied AI capabilities—ensuring alignment with institutional goals, compliance requirements, and the University’s evolving needs. Working in close partnership with senior leadership, key institutional stakeholders, and the Analytics & Data Science (ADS) team, the Executive Director leads the Data Engineering team in delivering integrated and high-performing data services that enable data-informed decision-making, operational excellence, and innovation across the University. A central focus of the role is designing, developing, and maintaining secure, scalable, and modern data and analytics systems using sound engineering methods. The Executive Director provides engineering oversight for enterprise software, data integration, and AI initiatives—ensuring the effective design, testing, and implementation of data pipelines, APIs, and analytical platforms that support institutional priorities. Additionally, this position leads the design, development, and governance of AI-enabled systems and applications, ensuring alignment with foundational IT infrastructure, data governance practices, and ethical AI standards. Key Responsibilities Lead the definition, engineering, and execution of the University’s enterprise data strategy, aligning data architecture, platforms, and AI capabilities with institutional goals and digital transformation initiatives. • Design, develop, and maintain robust data and analytics systems, ensuring scalability, security, and performance through modern engineering practices. • Oversee the Data Engineering team, responsible for enterprise data integration, warehousing, BI reporting, and advanced analytics capabilities. • Engineer and sustain a secure, scalable data-as-a-service environment to support operational reporting, advanced analytics, and AI workloads. • Provide technical leadership in software and systems engineering, including integration architecture, API design, and data pipeline development for enterprise systems such as Banner SaaS and Salesforce. • Oversee the full engineering lifecycle of data and analytics initiatives—from requirements analysis and system design through development, testing, deployment, and continuous improvement. • Collaborate with the ADS team to support advanced analytics, machine learning, and AI model integration within the enterprise data ecosystem. • Lead the engineering and governance of applied AI solutions, ensuring infrastructure, data readiness, and policies support responsible and effective AI adoption. • Establish and maintain data governance frameworks that ensure data quality, security, compliance, and accessibility across institutional systems. • Stay current with emerging trends in data engineering, BI, AI, and integration technologies to continually refine and modernize the University’s data strategy. • Foster a collaborative, high-performing engineering culture focused on innovation, service excellence, and continuous improvement. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Systems, Data Engineering, or a related field (Master’s degree preferred). • 10+ years of experience in data engineering, business intelligence, or enterprise data management, including 5+ years in a leadership role with system and software design oversight. • Proven experience designing and developing enterprise data systems, integrations, and analytics platforms using modern engineering principles. • Strong technical expertise in data architecture, APIs, middleware, and cloud-native solutions (experience with Microsoft Fabric highly desirable). • Experience with SaaS enterprise systems (e.g., Ellucian Banner, Salesforce) and enabling their reporting, analytics, and AI functionalities through secure integrations. • Knowledge of applied AI/ML technologies, including embedded and standalone capabilities within enterprise data environments. • Strong understanding of engineering best practices, including DevOps, CI/CD, version control, automated testing, and secure software development. • Demonstrated experience implementing data governance and compliance frameworks, ideally within higher education. • Exceptional strategic and operational leadership with the ability to bridge technical, business, and academic perspectives. • Prior experience in higher education or a similarly complex, data-intensive environment is highly desirable. The hiring salary range for this position is $120,000.00 - $130,000.00. The hiring salary range above represents the University's good faith estimate at the time of posting. Application Information Applicants must reside in the United States and be authorized to work in the U.S. If you experience any issues with the online submission process, please email recruitment@excelsior.edu . Excelsior University offers competitive compensation and a generous benefits package that includes paid time off, retirement, and excellent health insurance. Interested candidates should submit a letter of application, resume, and the names of three professional references. Please submit requested information by clicking the Apply Now button on this page. AA/EOE/ADA Excelsior University is an equal opportunity employer committed to ensuring all qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to any legally protected characteristic. Apply Now View All Jobs Jobs filler MyExcelsior Support Resources Areas of Study Tuition and Aid Admissions About Contact Us Jobs at Excelsior Excelsior University Main Campus 7 Columbia Circle Albany, NY 12203-5159 Educational Site 9400 4th Street N., Suite 100 St. Petersburg, FL 33702 © 2026 Excelsior University • Privacy • Policies • Transparency at Excelsior • Campus Safety • Title IX • Accommodations • Accessibility • Help • Feedback Start your degree with courses in Spanish. Learn about our ¡Adelante! program CLOSE Which language do you prefer? View our site in English or Spanish. English Español CLOSE Site Tools Stop Animations Start Animations Show Form Labels Hide Form Labels Accessibility at Excelsior We believe in education for all. Sitemap Technical Help Accessibility Statement More about Accessibility at Excelsior"
