s Undergraduate Associate in Science in Liberal Arts BS in Liberal Arts BS in Psychology Application Requirements Undergraduate International Hybrid & In-Person Learning Graduate Certificate Programs Career and Professional Skills Training Courses Nursing Nursing Undergraduate AAS in Nursing RN to BS in Nursing Jump Start RN to BS in Nursing BS in Nursing Hybrid Nursing Graduate RN to MS in Nursing Education RN to MS in Nursing Informatics RN to MS in Nursing Leadership and Administration of Health Care Systems MS in Nursing Education MS in Nursing Informatics MS in Nursing Leadership and Administration of Health Care Systems Application Requirements Associate Bachelor’s Master’s International Health Care Certifications Career and Professional Skills Training Courses Public Service Public Service Undergraduate AS in Criminal Justice BS in Criminal Justice BS in National Security Public Service Graduate Master of Public Administration (MPA) MS in Criminal Justice Graduate Certificate Programs Application Requirements Undergraduate & Graduate International Hybrid & In-Person Learning Career and Professional Skills Training Courses Technology Engineering Technology AAS in Technical Studies BS in Electrical Engineering Technology BS in Mechanical Engineering Technology BS in Nuclear Engineering Technology BPS in Technology Management Computer Technology AAS in Computer Technologies BS in Computer Science BS in Cybersecurity BS in Information Technology BPS in Information Technology Management MS in Cybersecurity Application Requirements Undergraduate & Graduate International Hybrid & In-Person Learning IT/Business Certifications Graduate Certificate Programs Technology Career Training Courses Courses Course Catalog Enrolled Student Course Registration Visiting and Non-Matriculated Student Course Registration Academic Calendar Noncredit Courses Career Advancement and Professional Skills Training Hybrid and In-Person Learning Admissions Admissions Overview Academic Calendar Start with More Credit Where to Send Your Transcripts Pursue Your Next Degree Application Requirements Business Health Sciences Liberal Arts Nursing Public Service Technology International Students Start Here Tuition and Aid Tuition Undergraduate Tuition Graduate Tuition Military Tuition Veteran Tuition Financial Aid NYS Free Tuition Eligibility Federal Financial Aid Steps to Apply for Financial Aid NY State Financial Aid for Residents Excelsior University Scholarships Grant and Private Loan Opportunities Resources Documents and Forms Payment Plans Resources Resources & Services Academic Calendar Accommodations for Students Bookstore & More Career Readiness Excelsior University Library Honor Societies at Excelsior National Cybersecurity Institute (NCI) Registration and Records Tech Support Web and Digital Accessibility The Writing Center Transcript Requests Online Transcript Request for Students and Alumni OneTranscript® Service for Non-Excelsior Students Military and Veteran Resources Military and Veteran Education Veterans Center Program Catalogs Catalogs Start With More Credit Start With More Credit ACE/Credly Transcripts Credit For Credit for Business and Professional Certifications Credit for Criminal Justice Training Credit for Educational and Vocational Programs Credit for Health Care Credentials Credit for IT Certifications, Training, and Exams Credit for Military Experience Credit For Nuclear Utility Accredited Training Programs Credit for Nursing Certifications and Licenses Credit for Professional and Workplace Training Credit for College and University Professional Training About Institutional Information About Excelsior About Our Students St. Petersburg Site Accreditations Contact Information Justice, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion Excelsior University EthicsHub Institutional Review Board Leadership Fast Facts George H. Atkinson Center at Excelsior University Media and Publications Life at Excelsior Blog Excelsior University Magazine Excelsior University Newsroom Faculty and Staff Published Works Academic Program Catalogs Center for Executive and Professional Education Center for Social Justice Calendar of Events Commencement Jobs at Excelsior University Policies and Guidelines Transparency Academic Transparency Administrative Transparency Regulatory Transparency Search search Fall II starts October 26. Ready to begin? Contact Admissions today. × Request Info Apply Call Us CLOSE Call Us For general inquiries, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Associate Director- Academic Evaluation Jobs at Excelsior University Associate Director- Academic Evaluation Status Full Time Location Albany, NY Apply Now View All Jobs The Associate Director of Academic Evaluation (ADAE) works closely with staff in the Registrar's Office, Advising Center, Admissions, and faculty and staff in academic units to support the effective operation of academic evaluation services. The ADAE assists in supervising and coordinating the work of academic evaluators, oversees daily workflow and caseload management, supports the implementation of unit goals and objectives, and contributes to quality assurance and continuous improvement initiatives. The ADAE serves as a resource for course classifications, degree program requirements, transfer credit policies, and academic evaluation procedures. This position facilitates communication among evaluators and collaborates with academic and administrative offices to promote consistency, efficiency, and excellent student service. This position requires the ability to analyze and apply complex academic policies consistently; excellent communication and leadership skills; and the ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with faculty, staff, and students. This full-time hybrid position, with a minimum of two required days at Excelsior's home office in Albany, NY, and the remainder of the days worked from home, reports to a Director of Academic Evaluation or the Associate Registrar within the Registrar's Office. Evening and weekend hours may be necessary for this position. Duties and Responsibilities: Assists in supervising and coordinating the work of a group academic evaluators through workflow management, training, coaching, and performance support. Monitors evaluator caseloads, work queues, and service metrics; recommends adjustments to ensure timely processing and achievement of departmental goals. Provides guidance to evaluators regarding academic policies, transfer credit decisions, degree requirements, and procedural questions. Assists with the development, implementation, and maintenance of policies, procedures, training materials, and evaluation resources. Assists in coordination of onboarding, training, and professional development activities for academic evaluation staff. Serves as a point of contact for escalated student, faculty, and staff inquiries related to academic evaluation and degree completion matters. Collaborates with faculty, deans, and university offices regarding curriculum changes and academic evaluation processes. Participates in university committees, work groups, and cross-functional initiatives that support student success and institutional effectiveness as needed. Assists with accreditation reviews, audits, and compliance-related activities by providing subject matter expertise. Represents Excelsior University at professional meetings, conferences, and external partner discussions as appropriate. Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Master's degree from an accredited institution 3-5 years of academic evaluation experience or equivalent experience in academic records, degree auditing, transfer credit evaluation, registrar services, or a related higher education function. Prior experience leading projects, coordinating teams, training staff, or providing supervisory oversight required Ability to manage multiple priorities, analyze complex information, meet deadlines, and maintain a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Demonstrated integrity, professionalism, sound judgment, and commitment to excellent student service. Strong analytical, problem-solving, organizational, and decision-making skills. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to interpret and apply university policies and procedures consistently and effectively. Proficient computer skills, including experience with student information systems, reporting tools, and Microsoft Office applications, with a willingness to learn new technologies. Preferred Qualifications: Formal supervisory experience preferred. The hiring salary range for this position is $62,500.00 - $70,000.00. The hiring salary range above represents the University's good faith estimate at the time of posting. Application Information Applicants must reside in the United States and be authorized to work in the U.S. If you experience any issues with the online submission process, please email recruitment@excelsior.edu . Excelsior University offers competitive compensation and a generous benefits package that includes paid time off, retirement, and excellent health insurance. Interested candidates should submit a letter of application, resume, and the names of three professional references. Please submit requested information by clicking the Apply Now button on this page. AA/EOE/ADA Excelsior University is an equal opportunity employer committed to ensuring all qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to any legally protected characteristic. Apply Now View All Jobs Jobs filler MyExcelsior Support Resources Areas of Study Tuition and Aid Admissions About Contact Us Jobs at Excelsior Excelsior University Main Campus 7 Columbia Circle Albany, NY 12203-5159 Educational Site 9400 4th Street N., Suite 100 St. Petersburg, FL 33702 © 2026 Excelsior University • Privacy • Policies • Transparency at Excelsior • Campus Safety • Title IX • Accommodations • Accessibility • Help • Feedback Start your degree with courses in Spanish. Learn about our ¡Adelante! program CLOSE Which language do you prefer? View our site in English or Spanish. English Español CLOSE Site Tools Stop Animations Start Animations Show Form Labels Hide Form Labels Accessibility at Excelsior We believe in education for all. Sitemap Technical Help Accessibility Statement More about Accessibility at Excelsior"
