sions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Military Billing Counselor Jobs at Excelsior University Military Billing Counselor Status Full Time Location Albany, NY Apply Now View All Jobs The Student Financial Services unit seamlessly delivers unparalleled service to both internal and external customers for financial aid, registration, student accounting, and veterans’ benefits. Team members are empowered to use independent judgment to respond to student needs. The Military Billing Counselor serves as a key liaison between the university and military-affiliated students, focusing primarily on processing Military Tuition Assistance (TA). This role ensures timely and accurate invoicing, reconciliation, and compliance with federal and Department of Defense (DoD) regulations. The counselor also provides guidance and support to military students regarding their tuition funding and billing questions. Additionally, this position may also be responsible for various processing requirements for each of the functional areas. We believe work should fit your life, not the other way around. Our hybrid schedule includes two days on site in our Albany office, with the flexibility to work remotely the remaining days. Spend less time commuting and more time focusing on meaningful work or personal priorities. Core hours are 8:30 AM–5:00 PM, including a 1-hour lunch, for a 37.5-hour week. Duties and Responsibilities: Review and process Military Tuition Assistance authorizations (e.g., ArmyIgnitED, MyCAA, Air Force, Navy, Marines, Coast Guard). Ensure correct tuition and fee rates are applied to student accounts in compliance with DoD policies and university procedures. Updating student accounts to ensure accurate tuition rates and adjusting accounts when needed. Reconcile student accounts related to TA payments; research and resolve discrepancies in a timely manner. Proactively monitor and track TA submissions to ensure timely processing prior to course start dates. Notify students of any missing documentation, incomplete TA forms, or discrepancies that may impact their billing or enrollment. Coordinate with academic departments to confirm course details, such as start/end dates and credit hours, required for TA authorization and invoicing. Stay informed of changes to DoD and service branch policies regarding TA eligibility, rates, caps, and invoicing requirements. Participate in ongoing training and compliance updates related to military education benefits and student account management. Act as point of contact on phones to counsel students. Assist with all assigned work queues, email and message center communications. Support the collection of required documentation and processing of forms related to Veterans Benefits and Tuition Assistance. Support the development of the whole student by providing excellent customer service and resolution of issues through telephone, email, and preparation of written correspondence. Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Associate degree in a relevant field "
    },
