 general inquiries, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Facilities Manager Jobs at Excelsior University Facilities Manager Status Full Time Location Albany, NY Apply Now View All Jobs The Facilities Manager ensures the efficient operation and safety of Excelsior University’s Albany campus. This role serves as the on-site point of contact, overseeing vendor services, space readiness, and compliance with safety standards. The Site Manager also supervises a small on-site team and coordinates with a property management company to maintain a professional and welcoming environment for staff and visitors. In addition, the site manager will serve as a point of contact for additional Excelsior University sites as they are established in regions throughout the United States. Duties and Responsibilities: Operational Oversight Act as the primary on-site contact for all campus operations, ensuring a safe, functional, and welcoming environment. Monitor and manage services provided by the property management company, including janitorial, landscaping, snow removal, and building maintenance. Respond to urgent site issues and coordinate emergency repairs with external vendors and management. Oversee main reception function for the institution, which includes walk in visitors, visitor and staff badge distribution, and main phone reception services. Oversee mailroom operations for the institution. Serve as a point of contact and subject matter expert for other Excelsior University sites who do not have full-time site managers. Space & Resource Management Coordinate space setup and vendor services for occasional on-site events and meetings. Preventive Maintenance & Compliance Ensure preventive maintenance schedules are followed by the property management team within budget guidelines. Maintain emergency preparedness plans (fire evacuation, disaster response) and serve as the site emergency coordinator. Promote good housekeeping and compliance with health, safety, and accessibility standards. Vendor & Contract Coordination Act as liaison for vendor relationships; review service reports and approve work orders in collaboration with property management. Assist with RFPs, bid reviews, and contract documentation as needed. Supervisory Responsibilities Supervise the receptionists, mailroom, and one facilities team member, providing scheduling, guidance, and performance feedback. Foster a positive and professional on-site experience for staff and visitors. Other Duties Serve as site backup coordinator onsite security concerns. Attend professional development opportunities as required. Perform additional responsibilities as assigned to support site operations. Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Education: Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in Facilities Management, Business Administration, or related field preferred. Experience: 3+ years of experience in facilities or site management, preferably in higher education or corporate environments. Experience supervising staff and managing vend"
