      "description": "Senior Associate Accreditation and State Relations | Excelsior Skip to main content Español Accessibility Sign In Military Air Force, Space Force, and Air National Guard Army & Army National Guard Marine Corps Military Family Members Coast Guard Navy Military Partners Veterans Lt. Col. Bryant A. Murray Veterans Center Veteran Partners Alumni Submit an Alumni Note Life at Excelsior Blog Career Readiness Center Alumni Leadership Council Become an Ambassador Alumni Awards Pay It Forward Giving Make A Gift Today Empower with Purpose How To Give Annual Giving at Excelsior Pay It Forward Endowed and Named Giving Opportunities Planned Giving Corporate and Other Ways of Giving Donor Recognition Partners Corporate Partners Association Partners Government Partners Community College and Other Academic Partners Find a Military and Veteran Representative Military, Spouse, and Veteran Partners Tuition Deferral Partner Scholarship Program Become a Partner Request Info Call Us Apply Areas of Study Business Business Undergraduate AAS in Administrative/Management Studies BPS in Business and Management BS in Business Business Graduate Doctor of Business Administration MBA MS in Human Resource Management with an Emphasis in Diversity and Technology MS in Management MS in Organizational Leadership with an Emphasis in Technology and Data Analytics Graduate Certificate Programs Application Requirements Undergraduate & Graduate International Students Start Here Hybrid & In-Person Learning IT/Business Certifications Business Career Training Courses Health Sciences Health Sciences Undergraduate AS in Health Sciences BS in Health Care Management BS in Health Sciences BS in Public Health Health Sciences Graduate MS in Health Sciences MS in Health Care Administration Graduate Certificate Programs Application Requirements Undergraduate & Graduate International Hybrid & In-Person Learning Health Care Certifications Health Care Career Training Courses Liberal Arts Liberal Arts Undergraduate Associate in Science in Liberal Arts BS in Liberal Arts BS in Psychology Application Requirements Undergraduate International Hybrid & In-Person Learning Graduate Certificate Programs Career and Professional Skills Training Courses Nursing Nursing Undergraduate AAS in Nursing RN to BS in Nursing Jump Start RN to BS in Nursing BS in Nursing Hybrid Nursing Graduate RN to MS in Nursing Education RN to MS in Nursing Informatics RN to MS in Nursing Leadership and Administration of Health Care Systems MS in Nursing Education MS in Nursing Informatics MS in Nursing Leadership and Administration of Health Care Systems Application Requirements Associate Bachelor’s Master’s International Health Care Certifications Career and Professional Skills Training Courses Public Service Public Service Undergraduate AS in Criminal Justice BS in Criminal Justice BS in National Security Public Service Graduate Master of Public Administration (MPA) MS in Criminal Justice Graduate Certificate Programs Application Requirements Undergraduate & Graduate International Hybrid & In-Person Learning Career and Professional Skills Training Courses Technology Engineering Technology AAS in Technical Studies BS in Electrical Engineering Technology BS in Mechanical Engineering Technology BS in Nuclear Engineering Technology BPS in Technology Management Computer Technology AAS in Computer Technologies BS in Computer Science BS in Cybersecurity BS in Information Technology BPS in Information Technology Management MS in Cybersecurity Application Requirements Undergraduate & Graduate International Hybrid & In-Person Learning IT/Business Certifications Graduate Certificate Programs Technology Career Training Courses Courses Course Catalog Enrolled Student Course Registration Visiting and Non-Matriculated Student Course Registration Academic Calendar Noncredit Courses Career Advancement and Professional Skills Training Hybrid and In-Person Learning Admissions Admissions Overview Academic Calendar Start with More Credit Where to Send Your Transcripts Pursue Your Next Degree Application Requirements Business Health Sciences Liberal Arts Nursing Public Service Technology International Students Start Here Tuition and Aid Tuition Undergraduate Tuition Graduate Tuition Military Tuition Veteran Tuition Financial Aid NYS Free Tuition Eligibility Federal Financial Aid Steps to Apply for Financial Aid NY State Financial Aid for Residents Excelsior University Scholarships Grant and Private Loan Opportunities Resources Documents and Forms Payment Plans Resources Resources & Services Academic Calendar Accommodations for Students Bookstore & More Career Readiness Excelsior University Library Honor Societies at Excelsior National Cybersecurity Institute (NCI) Registration and Records Tech Support Web and Digital Accessibility The Writing Center Transcript Requests Online Transcript Request for Students and Alumni OneTranscript® Service for Non-Excelsior Students Military and Veteran Resources Military and Veteran Education Veterans Center Program Catalogs Catalogs Start With More Credit Start With More Credit ACE/Credly Transcripts Credit For Credit for Business and Professional Certifications Credit for Criminal Justice Training Credit for Educational and Vocational Programs Credit for Health Care Credentials Credit for IT Certifications, Training, and Exams Credit for Military Experience Credit For Nuclear Utility Accredited Training Programs Credit for Nursing Certifications and Licenses Credit for Professional and Workplace Training Credit for College and University Professional Training About Institutional Information About Excelsior About Our Students St. Petersburg Site Accreditations Contact Information Justice, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion Excelsior University EthicsHub Institutional Review Board Leadership Fast Facts George H. Atkinson Center at Excelsior University Media and Publications Life at Excelsior Blog Excelsior University Magazine Excelsior University Newsroom Faculty and Staff Published Works Academic Program Catalogs Center for Executive and Professional Education Center for Social Justice Calendar of Events Commencement Jobs at Excelsior University Policies and Guidelines Transparency Academic Transparency Administrative Transparency Regulatory Transparency Search search Fall II late registration ends October 30. Ready to begin? Book an appointment with Admissions today. × Request Info Apply Call Us CLOSE Call Us For general inquiries, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Senior Associate Accreditation and State Relations Jobs at Excelsior University Senior Associate Accreditation and State Relations Status Full Time Location Remote | Albany, NY | Apply Now View All Jobs Excelsior University, a regionally accredited, online private not-for-profit institution of higher learning is seeking dynamic applicants for the position of Senior Associate Accreditation and State Relations in the Learning Outcomes and Quality Improvement unit. Learning Outcomes and Quality Improvement at Excelsior University works to ensure smooth institutional operations and integrity by enabling and supporting data-informed actions to enhance the learning environment for student success. This position coordinates institutional and programmatic accreditation activities and serves as the operational lead for state authorization, physical-presence, additional/site-location, and international regulatory compliance. The Senior Associate monitors requirements across U.S. jurisdictions, including obligations not covered by interstate reciprocity agreements, and coordinates registrations, applications, renewals, reports, disclosures, and responses. The role also supports compliance with applicable foreign ministries, governmental agencies, recognition bodies, accreditors, and quality-assurance organizations in Canada, Europe, and other countries. Working with academic leaders, legal counsel, compliance partners, finance, student-facing units, and affiliated entities, the Senior Associate will maintain authoritative records, assess regulatory impact, coordinate submissions and visits, and translate complex requirements into practical institutional action. This position is based out of the university’s home office in Albany, NY with the option of considering remote candidates. Remote employees will have mandatory occasional travel for meetings, conferences, and professional development opportunities. Remote employees are expected to be available during work hours 8:30am – 5:00pm Eastern time. The University will supply necessary equipment to perform the essential functions of this job (e.g., laptop, docking station). Employees are responsible for having a workspace where they can participate in virtual meetings without multiple interruptions and noise. Duties and Responsibilities: • Coordinate institutional and programmatic accreditation submissions, monitoring reports, substantive changes, evidence requests, reviews, and site visits. • Maintain a comprehensive inventory of approvals and obligations by state, jurisdiction, location, program, delivery activity, and affiliated entity. • Evaluate whether instructional activity, employees, recruitment, placements, residencies, facilities, or other operations create physical presence or authorization requirements. • Manage applications, registrations, exemptions, renewals, annual reports, fees, bonds, agents, and related documentation required by state agencies. • Oversee compliance for additional locations, instructional sites, and operations not covered by interstate reciprocity agreements. • Coordinate requirements imposed by foreign ministries, regulators, recognition bodies, accreditors, and quality-assurance organizations in Canada, Europe, and other jurisdictions. • Conduct regulatory due diligence for new programs, locations, partnerships, acquisitions, teach-outs, and geographic expansion. • Maintain authoritative compliance calendars, agency contacts, approvals, correspondence, and evidence repositories. • Coordinate accurate consumer, complaint, professional licensure, and location-related disclosures with legal, compliance, marketing, admissions, and academic partners. • Prepare responses to agency inquiries, complaints, audits, and information requests; coordinate corrective actions and document completion. • Monitor regulatory and accreditation changes using Statenet, and other regulatory monitoring resources, assess institutional impact, brief leadership, and recommend policy or operational updates. • Collaborate with LOQI team and institutional collaborators to support related accreditation and quality improvement-related initiatives. Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Earned master’s degree in an Educational or Social Science field with an emphasis on assessment. At least three years of experience working in accreditation, compliance, or institutional research/institutional effectiveness at an institution. Demonstrated experience interpreting and operationalizing state authorization, physical-presence, additional-location, or distance-education requirements. Experience preparing regulatory or accreditation applications, reports, substantive changes, and responses to external agencies. Excellent research, analytical, writing, project-management, organizational, and record-management skills. Ability to explain complex requirements clearly and lead cross-functional work involving academic, legal, financial, operational, and student-facing partners. Ability to manage multiple deadlines independently while maintaining accuracy, sound judgment, discretion, and timely escalation of risk. Preferred Qualifications: Experience managing multistate compliance for online, hybrid, and location-based education, including operations outside SARA coverage. Demonstrated success working effectively in a remote or hybrid environment. Experience with California postsecondary oversight and with Canadian, European, or other international regulatory or quality-assurance frameworks. The hiring salary range for this position is $90,000.00 - $106,000.00. The hiring salary range above represents the University's good faith estimate at the time of posting. Application Information Applicants must reside in the United States and be authorized to work in the U.S. If you experience any issues with the online submission process, please email recruitment@excelsior.edu . Excelsior University offers competitive compensation and a generous benefits package that includes paid time off, retirement, and excellent health insurance. Interested candidates should submit a letter of application, resume, and the names of three professional references. Please submit requested information by clicking the Apply Now button on this page. AA/EOE/ADA Excelsior University is an equal opportunity employer committed to ensuring all qualified applicants receive consideration for employment without regard to any legally protected characteristic. Apply Now View All Jobs Jobs filler MyExcelsior Support Resources Areas of Study Tuition and Aid Admissions About Contact Us Jobs at Excelsior Excelsior University Main Campus 7 Columbia Circle Albany, NY 12203-5159 Educational Site 9400 4th Street N., Suite 100 St. Petersburg, FL 33702 © 2026 Excelsior University • Privacy • Policies • Transparency at Excelsior • Campus Safety • Title IX • Accommodations • Accessibility • Help • Feedback Start your degree with courses in Spanish. Learn about our ¡Adelante! program CLOSE Which language do you prefer? View our site in English or Spanish. English Español CLOSE Site Tools Stop Animations Start Animations Show Form Labels Hide Form Labels Accessibility at Excelsior We believe in education for all. Sitemap Technical Help Accessibility Statement More about Accessibility at Excelsior"
    },
