s For general inquiries, Admissions, and Registrar's Office: 1.888.647.2388 Admissions Hours: Monday–Thursday 8:30 am–8 pm ET Friday 8:30 am–5 pm ET Saturday 8:30 am–12 pm ET Financial Aid Office 855.323.9235 International Students 1.518.464.8500 TDD 1.518.464.8501 CLOSE Sign In Options Application Portal Begin or continue your application MyExcelsior Enter your student portal Having Trouble? Visit our help page. CLOSE Search Searching... Frequently Asked Questions How many credits can I transfer? How much is tuition? How do I apply? How do I request a transcript online? How do I submit the TEAS test results? What is OneTranscript and how does it work? Is my employer an Excelsior University Partner? Jobs at Excelsior Who We Are Our Benefits See Yourself Here Infrastructure Engineer Jobs at Excelsior University Infrastructure Engineer Status Full Time Location Remote | Albany, NY | Apply Now View All Jobs We are seeking an infrastructure engineer with broad experience across various technologies to work in a complex and growing environment with a talented Infrastructure team. The Infrastructure Engineer is responsible for the support and organization of the Tier 3 Service Desk queue, as well as backup subject matter support in a number of technology areas depending on experience, including telephony, physical and cloud networking, Linux/Windows engineering, AWS and Azure administration. Reporting to the Sr. Director Infrastructure, this role helps ensure that various Excelsior platforms are secure, reliable, scalable, and aligned with institutional business objectives. The position provides engineering expertise, helps define and implement governance standards, supports automation initiatives, and partners with departments to modernize business processes. This role is focused on platform engineering, solution architecture, operational excellence, and user enablement within a complex enterprise environment. This position is based out of the university’s home office in Albany, NY with the option of considering remote candidates. Remote employees will have mandatory occasional travel for meetings, conferences, and professional development opportunities. Remote employees are expected to be available during work hours 8:30am – 5:00pm Eastern time. The University will supply necessary equipment to perform the essential functions of this job (e.g., laptop, docking station). Employees are responsible for having a workspace where they can participate in virtual meetings without multiple interruptions and noise. Duties and Responsibilities: Operate and improve cloud and hybrid infrastructure, including compute, storage, networking, telephony, identity, databases, backups, and monitoring. Apply sound administration practices across relevant Windows and Linux systems, virtualization platforms, and cloud services. Provision and maintain infrastructure through repeatable automation and infrastructure as code. Develop or maintain scripts, integrations, and event-driven workflows that reduce manual effort, improve consistency, and support safe change. Own complex Tier 3 incidents and escalations from triage through resolution. Analyze service desk and infrastructure trends to identify recurring incidents, emerging risks, capacity constraints, and noisy alerts. Maintain practical runbooks, knowledge articles, diagrams, configuration records, and change documentation. Improve incident, problem, and change workflows in alignment with ITIL/ITSM practices. Protect infrastructure through least-privilege access, secure configuration, patching, vulnerability remediation, backup and recovery practices, and audit-ready change records. Participate in risk reviews and continuity planning. Partner with service desk, application, infrastructure/security, and business teams to translate operational pain points into service improvements. Explain technical issues in clear language and share knowledge that raises the effectiveness of other support tiers. Qualifications: To perform t"
